{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_784174029#2_1503347350","relevance":3,"reason":"This article passage is dedicated to cultural diversity in nursing and directly explains its impact: culture affects patients' health beliefs, decisions, access, and barriers to appropriate care, and culturally competent nursing prepares nurses to address those differences.","learned":"Cultural diversity/EDI impacts nursing by helping nurses account for language, geography, socioeconomic status, gender, education, race/ethnicity, age, mental health, obesity, insurance, and access barriers that affect patient care decisions and appropriate care."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1436","reason":"The cultural diversity query is yielding directly relevant passages about how diversity affects nursing care, barriers, cultural competence, outcomes, and workforce; continue for more grade-3 evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1436"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_784174029#4_1503352397","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1436","rank":4,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_784174029#4_1503352397\" , \"end_char\": 5304.000000 , \"headings\": \"Understanding the True Importance of Cultural Diversity in Nursing Understanding the True Importance of Cultural Diversity in Nursing What Is Diversity Awareness? Aspects of <cover>Cultural Diversity in Nursing Culturally Competent Nurses Importance of a Culturally Diverse Nursing Workforce</cover>Learn More Recommended Readings: Sources \" , \"segment\": \"To better prepare for these situations, nurses follow a cultural competence model to identify their own cultural health care beliefs, gain knowledge and skills about caring for different cultural groups, and engage with diverse patients to practice their skills on an ongoing basis. These actions can reduce risks to patients by opening lines of communication, which can reduce medical errors and make it easier for providers to identify early indications of disease, according to a study in the journal Critical Care Clinics. Importance of a Culturally Diverse Nursing Workforce As the population of patients accessing health care services in the U.S. becomes increasingly diverse, providers will need to make significant changes in their approaches to care. A 2014 ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_784174029#3_1503349762","rank":3,"relevance":3}]}}
