{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_132634546#3_321966484","relevance":3,"reason":"This Fastaff article is dedicated to the importance of diversity in nursing and directly explains impacts: fairer access to jobs/promotions/benefits for nurses, peer support, better team evaluation and diagnosis, a better learning environment, and improved patient care through diverse perspectives.","learned":"Diversity/EDI impacts nursing by improving nurse opportunity and support, strengthening team decision-making and learning, and improving patient care through staff perspectives that reflect diverse communities."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"underrepresented minorities\" nursing (+ workforce diversity \"health equity\" \"patient care\" education barriers))","reason":"Search for additional evidence on underrepresented groups in nursing, workforce diversity, education barriers, health equity, and patient care impacts, aiming to find new sources beyond the already repeated diversity articles."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"underrepresented minorities\" nursing (+ workforce diversity \"health equity\" \"patient care\" education barriers))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_01_1795010691#9_2645640178","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1438","rank":2,"snippet":"Relationship Between Cultural Competence Education and Increasing Diversity in Nursing Schools and Practice Settings Abstract References \" , \"segment\": \"18 issue: 1_suppl, page (s): 28S-37S Issue published: January 1, 2007 Dula Pacquiao, EdD, RN, CTN University of Medicine and Dentistry of New Jersey PMID: 17204813 Abstract References Abstract This article attempted to examine the relationship between cultural competence education and increasing diversity in <cover>nursing schools and practice settings. In addition to the review of the literature, a panel of experts was interviewed regarding institutional practices in response to the challenge of increasing diversity and cultural competence education. Evidence of positive outcomes of cultural competent care and impact of race and ethnic concordance between patients and providers are presented. The challenge of increasing underrepresented minorities </cover>in health care professions remains elusive. An ecological analysis is recommended to address the social and cultural barriers that transcend the micro system of the school and the macro system of the society. The challenge of increasing diversity and realizing outcomes of cultural competence education requires social and comprehensive remedies to level life inequities that perpetuate a history of disadvantages in some groups.\" , \"start_char\":","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_01_1795010691#10_2645642071","rank":1,"relevance":3}]}}
